CHECKS: 5/7 passed
VERDICT: for the charged scalar in dS_4 the per-mode Bogoliubov factor is exp(-2 pi rho) cosh(pi(lam r + rho))/cosh(pi(lam r - rho)),
  rho^2 = lam^2 + mu^2 + 12 xi - 9/4.  At xi = 1/6, m = 0: rho^2 = lam^2 - 1/4 and the r = +-1 modes are exactly the dS_2 problem;
  off-axis r shifts lam -> lam r inside the cosh ratio only.  It depends on e only through lam (alpha free).  The pair number is
  singular as 1/rho at lam = lam_c (a threshold of the particle notion, not of the physics).  Scalar only; no claim about alpha.
